# lan-proof.inventory.example -- placeholder names only.
#
# One row per machine, whitespace separated:
#
#   label ssh-name role os iface uplink
#
#   label     the name on every result line; never a hostname
#   ssh-name  the name ssh would use; replace every .invalid name before a live run
#   role      server or client
#   os        linux, macos or windows
#   iface     the test interface
#   uplink    "-" or "uplink"; the xdp cell refuses an uplink interface
#
# The real inventory lives outside the repository.

# label     ssh-name            role    os      iface  uplink
server-a    server-a.invalid    server  linux   eth0   -
client-a    client-a.invalid    client  linux   eth0   -
client-b    client-b.invalid    client  linux   eth0   -
